  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This report is a literature review of quantum algorithms for derivative pricing and VaR, focusing on Quantum Accelerated Monte Carlo using amplitude estimation with theoretical complexity O(1/ε) versus classical Monte Carlo O(1/ε²). It surveys recent work including MLAE hardware tests on IBM and Honeywell devices (2–4 qubit circuits) and small demonstrations such as a 5‑qubit split‑step quantum walk for option pricing. The report concludes that noise and circuit‑depth limits prevent practical quantum advantage on current NISQ hardware.",
